.Sh DESCRIPTION
All "functions" mentioned here are passed as function pointers between
.Pa libcrypto
and the provider in
.Xr OSSL_DISPATCH 3
arrays, in the call of the provider initialization function.
See
.Xr provider 7
for a description of the initialization function.
They are known as "upcalls".
.Pp
All these "functions" have a corresponding function type definition
named
.Sy OSSL_FUNC_{name}_fn ,
and a helper function to retrieve the function pointer from a
.Xr OSSL_DISPATCH 3
element named
.Sy OSSL_FUNC_{name} .
For example, the "function"
.Fn core_gettable_params
has these:
.Bd -literal
 typedef OSSL_PARAM *
     (OSSL_FUNC_core_gettable_params_fn)(const OSSL_CORE_HANDLE *handle);
 static ossl_inline OSSL_NAME_core_gettable_params_fn
     OSSL_FUNC_core_gettable_params(const OSSL_DISPATCH *opf);
.Ed
.Pp
.Xr OSSL_DISPATCH 3
arrays are indexed by numbers that are provided as macros in
.Xr openssl-core_dispatch.h 7 ,
as follows:
.Pp
For
.Em in
(the
.Xr OSSL_DISPATCH 3
array passed from
.Pa libcrypto
to the provider):
.Bd -literal
